From e04839ec65b84766513aa3bc11502d9cdf25b724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SophiaWJ <jingwangsophia@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:01:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui_apple: premultiplied BGRA surfaces and per-frame surface
 reports

paint_surface took only 4:2:0 YCbCr video frames: the Metal renderer asserted
the format. A premultiplied BGRA pixel buffer (kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA), as
an external renderer draws into an IOSurface, now draws through its own
pipeline and shader with source factor one, so color where alpha is zero is
kept, as premultiplied compositing requires.

Such a buffer's owner must not draw into it again until GPUI has finished
reading it. metal_renderer::gpu_surfaces reports each frame that samples a
BGRA surface: the buffers it samples once its command buffer is encoded, and
the command buffer's completion with the GPU time it took. The hook is called
with the lock released, so it may replace itself from Metal's completion
thread.

The test renders a half-alpha red and an alpha-zero green BGRA surface beside
a gray YCbCr surface in one batch, headless, and checks the pixels and both
reports; a straight-alpha blend, a dropped report or a dropped YCbCr pipeline
bind fails it. A second test checks a hook can uninstall itself from inside
a report.

Release Notes:

- N/A
